## Phase 4: DOM System Investigation & Fixes
### 4.1 Unit Test Coverage for DOM Attributes ✅ COMPLETED
- [x] Investigate setAttribute/hasAttribute bug (hasAttribute returns false after setAttribute) - FIXED
- [x] Create DOM attribute unit tests (24 tests passing)
  - [x] Test setAttribute with empty string value
  - [x] Test setAttribute with non-empty string value
  - [x] Test hasAttribute after setAttribute
  - [x] Test getAttribute after setAttribute
  - [x] Test removeAttribute
  - [x] Test attribute enumeration (getAttributeNames)
  - [x] Test toggleAttribute
  - [x] Test hasAttributes
- [x] Investigate AttributeValue.From() behavior with empty strings - WORKS CORRECTLY
- [x] Verify Attr.Value assignment and retrieval - WORKS CORRECTLY

#### Bugs Fixed During Testing:
1. XMLCommon.Is_NameChar() was missing '-' and '.' characters per XML spec
2. OrderedDictionary.Remove() wasn't updating MapInverse (index mapping corruption)
3. OrderedDictionary.UpdateIndicesAfterRemoval() wasn't decrementing indices after removal
4. Element.toggleAttribute() was passing Document instead of Element as owner to Attr constructor
5. AttributeValue.Parse() wasn't handling custom/data-* attributes (returned null definition)

### 4.2 DOM Element Tests ✅ COMPLETED
- [x] Test element creation (createElement, createElementNS) - 14 tests passing
- [x] Test element hierarchy (appendChild, removeChild, insertBefore) - 34 tests passing
- [x] Test element queries (getElementById, getElementsByClassName, getElementsByTagName) - 21 tests passing
- [x] Test element matching (matches, closest, querySelector, querySelectorAll) - 22 tests passing

#### Bugs Fixed During Testing:
1. DOMCommon.createElementNS() was passing Prefix as Namespace parameter to Create_Element()
2. DOMImplementation.createHTMLDocument() was adding duplicate DOCTYPE (HTMLDocument already adds one)
3. TreeWalker.nextNode() wasn't advancing node to sibling after finding it
4. TreeWalker.filterNode() wasn't subtracting 1 from nodeType for bit mask calculation
5. DOMCommon.Is_Descendant() was using TreeWalker incorrectly (root can't traverse to ancestors)
6. Node.Dom_replace_node_within_parent() had validation checks in wrong scope (else instead of inside if parent is Document)

#### Bugs Fixed During Query/Matching Tests:
7. AttributeDefinition.Parse() for String type returned raw string instead of AtomicString (getElementById failed)
8. AttributeValue.Parse() had arguments in wrong order (Value/Data swapped)
9. AttributeValue.AsString() didn't handle AtomicString values (returned null)
10. AtomicString.GetHashCode() was returning hash of MemoryHandle instead of string content
11. Node.Dom_remove_node_from_parent() wasn't removing elements from Document's ID map
12. DOMCommon.Get_Elements_By_Qualified_Name() case-insensitive comparison was backwards
13. CssSelector.Match_Against_Tree() was adding LinkedListNode to another list (invalid operation)
14. Element.closest() was using TreeWalker incorrectly (skipped self, started from wrong node)
15. DOMCommon.Get_Ancestors() TreeWalker couldn't traverse ancestors (root was set to starting node)
16. ComplexSelector.Match() applied combinator from wrong selector (broke descendant/child matching)

